Prompt:

[Sport / Action]: {Whitewater kayaking, drifting, football, hurdles...}

[Environment]: {River rapids, mountain circuit, stadium, athletics track...}

[Main Headline]: {Your bold English title}

[Motion Interaction]: {Water flow, curved road, elastic net, track perspective...}

[Color Palette]: {High-contrast sports campaign colors}

[Brand / Tagline]: {Custom brand identity and slogan}

Create an explosive 9:16 vertical sports campaign poster combining high-speed action photography with giant perspective typography.

Capture the decisive moment of motion: a kayak cutting through rapids, a car drifting around a curve, a football striking the net, or an athlete clearing a hurdle.

Use cinematic low-angle photography, realistic motion, powerful lighting, and dramatic environmental depth.

Design enormous, ultra-bold sans-serif typography that follows the movement and geometry of the scene.

Stretch letters along perspective lines, bend them around curves, or let physical forces subtly distort their shapes. Integrate realistic interactions such as water splashes, tire smoke, stretched netting, and foreground obstacles.

Use exaggerated but coherent foreshortening to make the headline expand toward the viewer.

Maintain a strong balance between the moving subject and monumental lettering.

Complete the poster with clean top branding, vertical side information, and a concise bottom tagline.

Professional sports photography, dynamic composition, vivid contrast, and premium editorial design.

Keep all text accurate and readable. Avoid flat overlays, unrealistic motion, excessive CGI, and unnecessary decorations.

Prompt:

Theme: {theme}
Brand: {brand}
Product: {product}
Core word: {keyword}
Panel content: {5–7 related visual chapters}
Colors: {palette}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a premium spatial editorial poster using 5–7 freestanding visual panels with varied heights, widths, irregular silhouettes, and selected transparent materials.

Each panel should contain a meaningful part of the same theme: product, people, process, materials, environment, close-up details, or emotional imagery.

Arrange them with foreground, midground, and background depth, natural overlaps, realistic thickness, clean edges, and soft contact shadows.

Place one clear hero subject near the center. Integrate oversized {CORE WORD} typography behind and between the panels so it becomes part of the composition.

Use a clean light background, generous negative space, cohesive colors, realistic photography, and minimal editorial text.

Premium editorial design × spatial graphic design × product photography.

Avoid identical rectangular boards, rigid grids, miniature scenes, excessive props, clutter, random imagery, and cheap 3D mockup aesthetics.

Prompt:

[TITLE]: {fill in}
[LANDSCAPE]: {fill in}
[COLOR FIELD]: {fill in}
[MICRO NARRATIVE]: {fill in}
[SUBTITLE]: {fill in}
[HANDWRITTEN NOTE]: {fill in}
[FORMAT]: 9:16

Create a refined minimalist editorial poster on warm ivory fine-art paper.

Use one large irregular [COLOR FIELD] with subtle silkscreen, gouache and mineral-pigment texture. Add a very thin black [LANDSCAPE] with tiny [MICRO NARRATIVE] details to create a strong scale contrast.

Set “[TITLE]” in sophisticated editorial typography and add the subtitle “[SUBTITLE]”. Include sparse field-note information such as time, season, route, weather or distance, plus one small natural handwritten note: “[HANDWRITTEN NOTE]”.

Keep the hierarchy clear: large color field, tiny landscape, strong typography, micro information. The poster should feel minimal from far away but detailed up close.

Each new image should change the landscape structure, color-field direction, typography layout and narrative rather than simply swapping colors and titles.

Avoid flat vector shapes, cheap gradients, oversized scenery, random text, UI styling, dirty grunge texture, logos, watermarks, numbering, starbursts and sparkle symbols.

